+# Stage 19 Foundation Spine Acceptance Reconciliation
+
+## Decision
+
+The Foundation Spine package group (`19.1` through `19.5`) is accepted as a
+completed historical prerequisite for the narrow local project-open, bounded
+editing, durable-save, and normal-reentry sequence.
+
+This decision resolves the current-status ambiguity left by the Package `19.5`
+verification record. It does not amend that record, backdate human acceptance,
+or convert its focused automated evidence into release evidence.
+
+## Evidence boundary
+
+- Package `19.5` remains the immutable focused automated verification record.
+  It passed its bounded integrated-spine criteria at commit `9e99a335`.
+- Packages `19.18` and `19.20` later supplied broader manual and packaged
+  acceptance evidence for the V1 baseline.
+- This reconciliation relies on that later evidence only to confirm that the
+  Foundation Spine remained a valid prerequisite; it does not claim that
+  Package `19.5` itself performed manual acceptance, packaging, or release
+  qualification.
+
+## Status and limits
+
+```text
+FOUNDATION_SPINE_19_1_THROUGH_19_5: ACCEPTED_AS_NARROW_PREREQUISITE
+PACKAGE_19_5_AUTOMATED_VERIFICATION: PASS
+PACKAGE_19_5_MANUAL_ACCEPTANCE: NOT_CLAIMED
+PACKAGE_19_5_RELEASE_READINESS: NOT_CLAIMED
+STAGE_19: OPEN_PENDING_PACKAGE_19_22_CLOSURE
+```
+
+This record neither closes Stage 19 nor completes the internal V1 baseline.
+It authorizes no runtime work, release action, tag, signing request,
+publication, public distribution, or alpha/beta claim.
+
+## Reopening
+
+Reopen this reconciliation if the immutable Package `19.5` evidence is shown
+to be materially false, if a later accepted record contradicts its bounded
+project-open/save/reentry scope, or if a current authority record again states
+that Package `19.5` is awaiting acceptance.
